            <div xml:id="d709">

                <pb facs="0832" n="1666" xml:id="pg1666"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 652.119/507</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Spain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Willard</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Madrid</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-02-05T11:00:00+00:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">February 5, 1918, 11 a.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received February 6, 1.53
                        a.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1047. Supplementing Embassy’s 1042, February 4, 3 p.m., and referring directly to
                    Department’s 862, February 2, noon. It should be borne in mind that Spain does
                    not stand in the same relation to Central Powers as do northern neutral powers,
                    and that you can not deal with Spain unless her racial pride is considered. She
                    will never submit to rationing as suggested nor does Embassy feel that she will
                    agree to charter her shipping above national necessities. If the Department
                    decides to postpone permanent agreement until Spain feels more definitely
                    necessity of coming to agreement with us, such policy will be valueless so long
                    as Spanish Ambassador at Washington is able to secure permits to export all
                    commodities needed in Spain, notwithstanding our embargo, as is currently
                    reported here.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Willard</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
